eum located at the Akershus Fortress in Oslo. The museum collection focuses on Norwegian resistance during the occupation of Norway by Nazi Germany from 1940 to 1945. The museum displays equipment, photos and documents from the war years.","wpu":"Norway's Resistance Museum","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Hjemmefrontmuseet_Akershus.jpg/960px-Hjemmefrontmuseet_Akershus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Orlogsgast","g":"sights","k":"artwork","la":59.904802,"lo":10.737681,"d":276},{"n":"Defence Musuem","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":59.904511,"lo":10.740888,"d":281,"h":"May-Aug: Mo-Su 10:00-17:00; Sep-Apr: Mo-Su 10:00-16:00","w":"https://www.forsvarsbygg.no/festningene/Festningene/Akershus-festning/Museer-og-utstillinger/Forsvarsmuseet/","wp":"en:Armed Forces Museum (Norway)","ds":"The Armed Forces Museum of Norway (Norwegian: Forsvarsmuseet - The Defence Museum) is a museum located at Akershus Fortress in Oslo, Norway. Previously it was named Hærmuseet, The Army Museum (even earlier the Artillery Museum). The museum consists of mostly army materiel.","wpu":"Armed Forces Museum (Norway)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Hovedarsenalet_Akershus.jpg/960px-Hovedarsenalet_Akershus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Festningen Restaurant utsiktspunkt","g":"sights","k":"viewpoint","la":59.907834,"lo":10.735182,"d":284},{"n":"Kreftforeningens Vitensenter","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":59.909817,"lo":10.741857,"d":329,"w":"https://kreftforeningen.no/vitensenteret/"},{"n":"Tegnerforbundet","g":"sights","k":"gallery","la":59.909961,"lo":10.740994,"d":333,"h":"Tu-Fr 12:00-17:00; Sa-Su 12:00-16:00"},{"n":"K7 Hotel Oslo","g":"sights","k":"hotel","la":59.909947,"lo":10.741406,"d":336,"w":"https://k7hotel.com/","ph":"+47 23 10 08 00","wifi":1},{"n":"The Mini Bottle Gallery","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":59.909641,"lo":10.743402,"d":