ershus Fortress","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":59.906667,"lo":10.736111,"d":219,"ds":"Akershus Fortress or Akershus Castle (Norwegian: Akershus slott [ɑkəʂˈhʉːs ˈslɔtː]) is a medieval castle in the Norwegian capital Oslo that was built to protect and provide a royal residence for the city. It is located on the banks of the Oslofjord.","wpu":"Akershus Fortress","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/14-09-02-oslo-RalfR-370.jpg/960px-14-09-02-oslo-RalfR-370.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Havnelageret","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":59.907608,"lo":10.746667,"d":377,"ds":"Havnelageret (also known as Oslo Havnelager), literal translation \"The harbour warehouse\", is a commercial building located at Langkaia 1 in Oslo, Norway. It houses Norwegian Defence Estates Agency as tenants.","wpu":"Havnelageret","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/cc/Havnelageret_Oslo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Vippetangen","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":59.902885,"lo":10.741861,"d":469,"ds":"Vippetangen is the southern tip of the Akersnes peninsula in central Oslo, Norway, located southeast of Akershus Fortress and bounded on three sides by the Oslofjord. It has in the past served as an important part of the port of Oslo. The area is currently undergoing urban renewal as part of the Fjord City development.","wpu":"Vippetangen","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Vippetangen.jpg/960px-Vippetangen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Egertorget","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":59.9128,"lo":10.7419,"d":653,"ds":"Egertorget is a pedestrian mall located at the intersection of Karl Johans gate and Øvre Slottsgate in Oslo, Norway.","wpu":"Egertorget","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Egertorget_Oslo.jpg/960px-Egertorget_Oslo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Eidsvolls plass","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":59.9133,"lo":10.739,"d":702,"ds":"Eidsvolls plass (\"Eidsvoll Square\") is a square and park in Oslo, Norway, located west of the Parliament of Norway Building, south of Karl Johans gate and east of Studenterlunden and the National Theatre. It has been referred to as \"the National Mall of Norway\".","wpu":"Eidsvolls plass","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Storting_Spring_2016.JPG/960px-Storting_Spring_2016.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Stortorvet","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":59.91277,"lo":10.74546,"d":710,"ds":"Stortorvet ('The Grand Plaza') is a square in Oslo, Norway, located west of Oslo Cathedral.","wpu":"Stortorvet","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Christian_IV_av_CL_Jacobsen_1.jpg/960px-Christian_IV_av_CL_Jacobsen_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Deutsches Theater (Oslo)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":59.9133,"lo":10.7357,"d":740,"ds":"Deutsches Theater was a German-language theater in Oslo, Norway which existed between 1941 and 1944, during the German occupation of Norway. It was established on 1 January 1941 following an order from Josef Terboven, and the first performance was held on 22 April 1941 in Nationaltheatret. It later moved to new localities, in Stortingsgata 16.","wpu":"Deutsches Theater (Oslo)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Stortingsgata_16_Oslo.jpg/960px-Stortingsgata_16_Oslo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Oslo Opera House","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":59.906944,"lo":10.753611,"d":758,"ds":"The Oslo Opera House (Norwegian: Operahuset) is the home of the Norwegian National Opera and Ballet, and the national opera house in Norway. The building is situated in the Bjørvika neighbourhood of central Oslo, at the head of the Oslofjord. It is operated by Norwegian Directorate of Public Construction and Property, the government agency which manages property for the Norwegian government.","wpu":"Oslo Opera House","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Oslo_Opera_House_-_2025.jpg/960px-Oslo_Opera_House_-_2025.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Oslo is the capital and largest city of Norway. It constitutes both a county and a municipality. The municipality of Oslo had a population of 724,290 in 2025, while the city's greater urban area had a population of 1,110,887 in 2025, and the metropolitan area had an estimated population of 1,546,706 in 2021.","wpu":"Oslo","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Nationaltheatret_evening.jpg/960px-Nationaltheatret_evening.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}